WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.276 --> 00:00:03.359
(upbeat dance music)

00:00:04.235 --> 00:00:05.454
- Oh, it's a nice place.

00:00:05.454 --> 00:00:06.917
- Yeah, crazy how empty it is

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:09.007
for a Tuesday afternoon, though.

00:00:09.007 --> 00:00:10.632
- What can I get you gentlemen?

00:00:10.632 --> 00:00:12.385
- We will have two beers.

00:00:12.385 --> 00:00:13.488
- Oh, no, no, no.

00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:15.566
We only serve wine here.

00:00:15.566 --> 00:00:17.482
- What am I, at my parents'?

00:00:17.482 --> 00:00:18.823
I've never had wine before.

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:19.864
(gasps)

00:00:19.864 --> 00:00:22.697
(easy rock music)

00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:30.685
- I have tasted the forbidden fruit.

00:00:30.685 --> 00:00:33.175
- With some sort of
child sacrifice for this.

00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:34.243
- What year was this bottled?

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:36.681
I won't drink anything younger than 1800.

00:00:36.681 --> 00:00:39.131
- I want seven pounds of a cheese platter.

00:00:39.131 --> 00:00:41.453
- You can really taste
the notes of chocolate.

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:43.090
- I'm picking up hint of rocky road.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.355
- Do you think maybe
it's because we visited

00:00:44.355 --> 00:00:46.224
an ice cream parlor beforehand?

00:00:46.224 --> 00:00:48.059
- Look at me, I'm a wine-nocerous.

00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:48.892
Get it?

00:00:48.892 --> 00:00:50.346
- This wine has a great set of legs,

00:00:50.346 --> 00:00:52.227
like our model friend Heidi Klum.

00:00:52.227 --> 00:00:53.945
(gargles)

00:00:53.945 --> 00:00:55.373
That's good.

00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:58.101
Ooh, what a fantastic
sauvignon blanc we're having.

00:00:58.101 --> 00:00:59.530
- I love savi-nom-nom.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.389
(laughs)

00:01:00.389 --> 00:01:02.223
- I am so funny when I drink wine.

00:01:02.223 --> 00:01:03.814
I should be on David Letterman.

00:01:03.814 --> 00:01:05.822
- You're funnier than my court jester.

00:01:05.822 --> 00:01:07.839
- Look at us just drinking
some gossip juice.

00:01:07.839 --> 00:01:11.055
- Loose lips sink ships, and
I'm the captain of the Titanic.

00:01:11.055 --> 00:01:13.667
- Did I tell you my son
Preston got suspended

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.746
from Academy again for
saying the word "sexy"

00:01:15.746 --> 00:01:16.883
too much in class?

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:18.927
- Did you hear that
Brenda's husband got kicked

00:01:18.927 --> 00:01:20.273
out of the country club because

00:01:20.273 --> 00:01:22.395
he only tipped the caddy $50.

00:01:22.395 --> 00:01:23.498
- Again?

00:01:23.498 --> 00:01:24.331
- Again.

00:01:24.331 --> 00:01:25.164
- Uh oh!

00:01:25.164 --> 00:01:27.692
Looks like I'm about to
send an e-mail to my ex.

00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:28.551
- What did he say?

00:01:28.551 --> 00:01:31.586
- What do you mean you
want to meet tonight?

00:01:31.586 --> 00:01:33.618
Look at me, I'm crying like a poor person.

00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:36.390
- Does anyone have a hundred
dollar bill to blow my nose?

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.073
- I am not an alcoholic if it's wine.

00:01:38.073 --> 00:01:39.257
Wine is good for you.

00:01:39.257 --> 00:01:41.127
- We're never going to die.

00:01:41.127 --> 00:01:41.960
(laughs)

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:42.845
(puking)
You're all right,

00:01:42.845 --> 00:01:43.988
you're all right, buddy.

00:01:43.988 --> 00:01:45.288
- Hold my hair back.

00:01:45.288 --> 00:01:46.960
(puking)

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.043
(upbeat dance music)

